.SH "NAME"
pcre2_convert_context_free \- free a convert context
.SH "SYNOPSIS"
.sp
.ss \n[.ss]
.nf
.fam C
\fB\&#include\fP \fB<pcre2.h>\fP

\fBvoid\fP pcre2_convert_context_free(\fBpcre2_convert_context\fP *\fIccontext\fP);
.fam
.fi
.ss \n[.ss] 0
.SH "DESCRIPTION"
.sp
This function is part of an experimental set of pattern conversion functions.
It frees the memory occupied by a convert context, using the memory
freeing function from the general context with which it was created, or
\f(CRfree()\fP if that was not set. If the argument is \fBNULL\fP, the function returns
immediately without doing anything.
.sp
The pattern conversion functions are described in the
\f(CRpcre2convert\fP
documentation.